url: "https://github.com/ANR-MAMUT/MAMUT-routing-Poryos2026"
abstract: >-
  Poryos2026 is an original benchmark family proposed by the listed authors and generated from OpenStreetMap road networks in 5 cities. Its design combines customer sampling, generated routing attributes, alternative arc-cost metrics, time-window variants and controlled synthetic traffic. Shared base instances yield paired CVRP, VRPTW, TDVRP and TDVRPTW variants for studying the effects of time dependence and congestion. OpenStreetMap and its contributors provide the underlying geographic data.
